    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Borgman Earls are delighted to present Greenbank, Stradbrook Road to the rental market – a spacious four-bedroom semi-detached home offering the space, flexibility and garden that can be difficult to find in the Blackrock rental market.\r\n\r\nThe property is being offered UNFURNISHED. Please note that the furniture and personal belongings shown in the photographs will not form part of the tenancy.\r\n\r\nSet elevated and back from Stradbrook Road, Greenbank is a mature home with ample off-street parking to the front and a particularly generous private garden to the rear.\r\n\r\nInside, the accommodation is bright & comfortable.\r\n\r\nThe entrance hall, with its original-style parquet flooring, leads through to a generous living room overlooking the front garden. This connects directly with a second reception room, currently being used as a children's play and games room. It could work equally well as a more formal dining room, second sitting room or home office, depending on the needs of the incoming tenants.\r\nTo the rear is a separate fitted kitchen which in turn opens into a large extended dining area. With windows running along much of the room and views directly over the garden, this is a great everyday space with plenty of room for a large dining table and additional furniture.\r\nThe extension also provides direct access to the rear garden.\r\nThere is access from the entrance hall into the adjoining garage, providing very useful additional storage for bikes, sports equipment, and garden furniture.\r\n\r\nUpstairs there are four bedrooms, including two particularly generous double bedrooms, together with two further bedrooms offering good flexibility for children, guests or working.\r\n\r\nOutside, the rear garden is a real feature of the property. It is large, private and predominantly laid to lawn, providing plenty of space for children to play. There is also a patio area to the side, ideal for outdoor dining during the warmer months.\r\n\r\nFor people looking to rent in the Blackrock area, the location is likely to be a major attraction. Greenbank is conveniently positioned close to Blackrock, Monkstown and Deansgrange, with an excellent choice of local shops, cafés, parks, sporting facilities and everyday amenities nearby. The area is particularly well served by a wide selection of primary and secondary schools, while public transport and access to surrounding South Dublin areas are also within easy reach.\r\n\r\nFour-bedroom homes are not always easy to find on the rental market in this part of South Dublin, particularly homes offering this combination of living space, parking, storage and a large private garden.\r\nGreenbank is a comfortable and well-located home that should appeal to people looking to put down roots in the area and enjoy everything Blackrock and its surrounding neighbourhoods have to offer."
      },
